---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="Website privacy policy"
  description="Privacy policy for sourcedwriter.com and the plugin's optional usage data: analytics only with your consent, no forms or ads."
  schema={[breadcrumbNode([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Website privacy', path: '/privacy/' }])]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Website privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated 7 October 2026</p>

      <p>
        This policy covers the website {SITE.domain} and the optional usage data the WordPress plugin can send to it. For
        everything else the plugin sends and stores, see
        <a href="/docs/privacy-and-external-services/">Privacy and external services</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        The site is a set of static pages with no forms or ads. If you consent, it uses Google Analytics to count visits and
        see which pages are read.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Google Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics runs only if you choose Accept in the cookie banner. Until then no analytics script is loaded
        and no cookies are set. Your choice is saved in your browser's local storage for up to a year.
        <a href="#cookies" data-consent-open>Change your cookie settings</a> at any time; withdrawing consent deletes
        the analytics cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        When accepted, Google Analytics sets cookies and collects data such as pages viewed, referring site, approximate location,
        device and browser type. Google processes this data on the site's behalf. See
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
        You can also block it with a browser setting, a content blocker or the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log technical data such as visitor IP addresses for security and
        to run the service. See the
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="plugin-usage-data">Plugin usage data</h2>
      <p>
        From version 1.5, an administrator of a site running the plugin can choose to share anonymous usage data. It is off
        by default. When it is on, the site sends a daily batch of events to telemetry.{SITE.domain}, such as which AI provider
        is used, whether drafts finish, and which errors occur, as described in
        <a href="/docs/privacy-and-external-services/#usage-data">the full list of events</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The data contains no site address, names, email addresses, user or post IDs, API keys, or anything written in the
        plugin. Each site is identified only by a random install ID created when usage data is turned on. It is used only to
        improve the plugin, never sold or shared, and never combined with this website's analytics.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is received by a Cloudflare Worker and stored in a Cloudflare D1 database. Cloudflare processes the request,
        including the sending server's IP address, in transit; the service does not store IP addresses or request headers,
        and request logs are off. See the
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>. Events are kept for 24 months,
        then deleted; totals that contain no install IDs may be kept longer.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site's administrator can turn usage data off at any time in Settings → Usage data, and delete everything sent
        from their site with Diagnostics → Usage data → Delete data on server. You can also email the install ID shown there
        to {SITE.contactEmail} to have it deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email {SITE.contactEmail}, your message and address are used only to reply to you and, if you asked, to
        tell you about launches. They aren't sold or shared, and you can ask for them to be deleted at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Controller: {SITE.author.name}. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
